  "answer":"No. The current release policy does not allow a model to be promoted based solely on accuracy exceeding 0.80. The legacy rule that used an accuracy > 0.80 is explicitly superseded. Today a release requires evaluation on a frozen holdout and promotion only when the model’s F1 score improves by at least 0.005 and its ROC‑AUC does not drop by more than 0.01. Therefore an accuracy above 0.80 alone does not authorize a release today.",
  "sources":[
    {
      "source_id":"legacy-policy",
      "quote":"The old 2024 process promoted any model when accuracy exceeded 0.80. It is superseded by release-policy: current releases use F1 and ROC-AUC on a frozen holdout."
    },
    {
      "source_id":"release-policy",
      "quote":"Production model changes require an evaluation on a frozen holdout. Promote only when F1 improves by at least 0.005 and ROC-AUC drops by no more than 0.01."
    }
  ]
}
